      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The discriminant is \\[ p^2-4\\left(\\frac{p^2-1}{4}\\right)=1. \\] The roots are \\(\\frac{p+1}{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{p-1}{2},\\) whose difference is \\(1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
